  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "setup-notes",
      "page": "setup",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1280,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Setup flow. The TV only needs input to start the room; after that the VIP (first phone to join) runs everything from their phone, and the TV mirrors what they pick.\nAll names, the room code and the QR are sample content."
    },
    {
      "id": "imposter-notes",
      "page": "imposter",
      "x": 6120,
      "y": 1280,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Imposter, one word shown end to end: Priya holds the decoy (ZEBRA), the crew has GIRAFFE.\n\nAssumptions to check:\n- The speaker taps \"I'm done\" to pass the turn, or the timer runs out.\n- You can vote for anyone but yourself.\n- The crew's word stays hidden on the TV until the imposter's last guess is in.\n- Point values are placeholders until the spec sets scoring.\n- Not drawn yet: the round where the imposter escapes the vote."
    },
    {
      "id": "real-or-nah-notes",
      "page": "real-or-nah",
      "x": 4080,
      "y": 1280,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Real or Nah, one fact shown end to end.\n\nAssumptions to check:\n- The reveal puts everything on one screen here; the build can play it lie by lie.\n- Answers appear in the same shuffled order on the TV and every phone.\n- Point values are placeholders until the spec sets scoring."
    },
    {
      "id": "end-notes",
      "page": "end-system",
      "x": 1000,
      "y": 1280,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "End of a game and the system states. Bracketed items on the credits and full-tonight screens are real facts still to fill in (repo URL, music, sound effects)."
    },
    {
      "id": "style-intro",
      "page": "style-options",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -260,
      "w": 1100,
      "text": "The two style options that weren't picked, kept for reference. Doodle Notebook (option C) is now the main set on the other pages."
    },
    {
      "id": "direction-a",
      "page": "style-options",
      "x": 2530,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "A \u00b7 Sticker Shop\nThick ink outlines, hard offset shadows, flat bold colors on warm cream. Lilita One + Nunito."
    },
    {
      "id": "direction-b",
      "page": "style-options",
      "x": 2530,
      "y": 1320,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "B \u00b7 Saturday Morning\nDeep grape stage, candy-colored bubbles, no outlines. Titan One + Baloo 2."
    },
    {
      "id": "no-tv-notes",
      "page": "no-tv",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1180,
      "w": 1100,
      "text": "No-TV mode: no shared screen anywhere. Every phone carries the shared stage on top and that player's own controls below.\n\nTop row is the platform: starting a room from a phone, the room code read aloud, and a game that needs a TV shown disabled rather than hidden.\nSecond row is Imposter in phase order. Word check deliberately shows an empty stage \u2014 a phase shows the stage or your secret, never both.\n\nPhones are silent here, haptics only, so the Suspense ring on Reveal and Last chance is the visual standing in for the drumroll.\nAll names, the room code and the words are sample content."
    },
    {
      "id": "doodle-bluff-notes",
      "page": "doodle-bluff",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1240,
      "w": 1100,
      "text": "Doodle Bluff. Everyone draws two secret prompts up front, then drawings are shown one at a time: everyone but the artist writes a fake title, then the room votes for the real one.\n\nThe six marker inks are settled here, contrast-checked against the paper. Colour is decoration only \u2014 no rule, score, title or vote ever reads a stroke's colour.\n\nThe gallery is the finale: every drawing made in the game, including the ones never titled, and then they die with the room.\nAll names, prompts and titles are sample content."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "setup"
  }
}
